dialogue trust_sage_3
title: The first knot
trigger: Trust sage level=3
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Sage has the satchel open on a flat stone and every jar out of it in a row, and is sorting them again, though they were sorted at dusk.
  * Something missing from the satchel? -> missing
    do: AddTrust $with 4
  * You sorted those an hour ago. -> sorted
    do: AddTrust $with -2
  * Leave the jars. Tell me what's wrong. -> wrong
    do: AddTrust $with 5

node missing hero
  No. Everything's here. That's the trouble with a satchel. It's always got everything in it except the one thing.
  -> first

node sorted hero
  I did. Hands like to be busy when the head won't be. You'd know, if you ever sat still.
  -> first

node wrong hero
  Straight to it. All right. Nothing's wrong tonight. Something was wrong a long time ago, and tonight it's loud.
  -> first

node first commander
  The Sage pulls the cord from a sleeve and holds up the first knot on it, the oldest, worn almost smooth.
  -> wick

node wick hero
  This one's Wick. My apprentice, off the Lantern Road. Wick came to the city with me to learn what the neon does with mana. Quick hands. Better at the salves than I ever was.
  -> thin

node thin hero
  Then Wick's colour started going thin. You'll have seen it in the cities. The glow in the heartbeat fades a little more each week, and nothing in this satchel puts it back. I tried every jar. Twice.
  -> stair

node stair hero
  The Choir told Wick the Lullaby at the top of the spire would make it whole again. So Wick climbed. I tied the knot the morning after. I didn't tie it before. I was so sure I'd mend it first.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Sage turns the knot between finger and thumb and doesn't look up.
  * If there's any trace of Wick at the top, we bring it down. I promise you that. -> promised
    do: AddTrust $with 10
    do: SetFlag sage:wick_promised
  * You couldn't mend what the Choir did. That was never yours to carry. -> absolved
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag sage:wick_absolved
  * Wick chose the stair. Let Wick's choice be Wick's. -> chose
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag sage:wick_chose

node promised hero
  A promise. From somebody climbing the same stair. That's either the bravest thing I've heard or the most foolish, and on the road those come out the same. I'll hold you to it.
  -> after

node absolved hero
  Never mine. I've said that to a hundred people at a hundred bedsides. It's strange how little it helps when it's turned round. But it helps a little. Thank you.
  -> after

node chose hero
  Wick's choice. Yes, it was. Wick was grown, and stubborn, and wanted to be whole. I just thought I'd have the last word. Healers always think that. I'll climb with you anyway, Commander.
  -> after

node after commander
  The Sage puts the jars back one by one, the right way round this time, and buckles the satchel shut.
  -> close

node close hero
  Nobody climbs alone. The road says it over every lantern. Wick did, though. I don't mean to let that happen twice.
